# Phase Document Standards

## File Naming

Phase files live in `docs/phases/` and follow this naming convention:

```
phase-<N>-<kebab-case-title>.md
```

Examples:
- `phase-0-project-setup.md`
- `phase-8-jira-draft-extraction.md`
- `phase-17-integrate-task-manager.md`

- Use **global** phase numbers (0-based, sequential across the whole roadmap),
  not local sub-phase numbers.
- Never use spaces in filenames. Replace spaces with hyphens.

## Phase Numbering Reference

Always use **global phase numbers** when referencing another phase inside a
document. Never use "phase 1" to mean "the first Jira phase" — use the actual
global number (e.g. "Phase 8").

Current global phase map:

| N | Theme |
|---|-------|
| 0 | Project setup |
| 1 | MVP core flow |
| 2 | Database integration |
| 3 | Cloud storage |
| 4 | Deployment & infrastructure |
| 5 | Async processing (BullMQ) |
| 6 | Testing & QA |
| 7 | Security & performance |
| 8 | Jira draft extraction |
| 9 | Multi-project Jira |
| 10 | Roles and approval permissions |
| 11 | SUPERADMIN and organizations |
| 12 | Meeting platform integration (Zoom) |
| 13 | MCP and existing issue lookup |
| 14 | Payment gateway |
| 15 | Advanced features (real-time, analytics) |
| 16 | Monitoring and maintenance |
| 17 | Extended task manager integrations |
| 18 | Future architecture and scale |

## Document Structure

For **implementation-ready phases** (8 and beyond), use this structure:

```markdown
# Phase N: Title

## Goal
One paragraph. What this phase achieves and why it matters.
State explicitly what is NOT being built (scope boundary).

## Before you start
Numbered list of things to read or verify in the existing codebase
before writing any code. Prevents building on wrong assumptions.

## What to build

### 1. <Component / feature name>
- Bullet points describing what to build.
- Reference exact file paths, entity names, column names, and
  method signatures where known.
- If a design decision has trade-offs, state them and pick one.

### 2. <Next component>
...

## New module structure (if applicable)
ASCII tree of new files/directories to create.

## Technologies & Tools (if new dependencies are introduced)
Table or list of new packages with brief justification.

## Dependencies
List of global phases that must be complete before this phase starts.

## Explicitly out of scope for this phase
Bullet list of things that were considered but deferred. This prevents
scope creep during implementation.

## Acceptance criteria
Numbered list of testable conditions that define "done".
Each criterion must be verifiable without reading the source code.
```

For **early setup phases** (0–7) or phases that are already complete,
the existing structure (with `## Verification Checklist`) is acceptable.

## Style Rules

- Use **global phase numbers** in all cross-references (e.g. "Phase 11", not "phase 4").
- Use backtick formatting for: entity names, column names, file paths, env vars,
  method names, TypeScript types, and CLI commands.
- Use snake_case for database column names, camelCase for TypeScript properties.
- Keep "Explicitly out of scope" sections honest — list things that were
  actually considered and deferred, not an exhaustive list of everything
  not built.
- Acceptance criteria must be **testable** — avoid vague criteria like
  "the feature works correctly". Prefer "A USER cannot call the approve endpoint
  and receives a 403 response."
- Do not add emojis.

## Architecture Docs

Architecture documentation lives in `docs/architecture/` and is separate from
phase docs. Phase docs describe **what to build and when**; architecture docs
describe **how the system works now**.

When a phase introduces a significant new pattern (new entity, new queue, new
auth mechanism), update the relevant architecture doc alongside the phase doc.

| Architecture doc | Update when |
|-----------------|-------------|
| `overview.md` | New feature module or infrastructure component added |
| `data-flow.md` | New request flow or ingestion path |
| `database-schema.md` | New entity or significant schema change |
| `async-processing.md` | New queue or processor |
| `security.md` | New auth mechanism, guard, or credential type |
| `integrations.md` | New external service integrated |
